==English==
{{wikipedia|lang=en}}
[[File:Ceres symbol.svg|thumb|65px|Ceres astronomical symbol]]

===Etymology===
{{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|Cerēs}}, goddess of the bounty, akin to {{m|la|crēare||to create}}, {{m|la|crēscere||to grow}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*ḱer-||to grow}}. More at [[create]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈsɪəɹiːz/|lang=en}}
* {{hyphenation|Ce|res|lang=en}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{senseid|en|Q32102}}{{lb|en|Roman god}} The Roman [[goddess]] of [[agriculture]]; equivalent to the [[Greek]] goddess [[Demeter]].
# {{senseid|en|Q596}}{{lb|en|astronomy}} A celestial body [[orbit]]ing between [[Mars]] and [[Jupiter]], the largest [[asteroid]] and innermost [[dwarf planet]]; officially called {{m|mul|1 Ceres|1 '''Ceres'''}}.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|astronomy}} {{l|en|1 Ceres}}, [[⚳]]

